course: dictionary
lesson: 14445
title: A pang is a sudden feeling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pang is a sudden feeling that arrives quickly and often does not last long. «Sam felt a sharp pang in his tummy and remembered he had skipped lunch.» The word sharp and the missed lunch are your clues: a pang is a sudden, sharp pain.
explain: A pang can also be a feeling, not just a pain. «When Mia saw her friend's new bike, she felt a pang of envy.» Envy means wanting what someone else has, so a pang of envy is a sudden, strong jealous feeling. Check it: swap in "a sudden strong feeling" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Pangs is the plural, so one pang becomes more than one pangs. Phrases like «hunger pangs», «a pang of guilt» and «a pang of regret» show you what kind of feeling is meant. Read the words around pang to find out which one it is.
fact: Pang is a noun. You can have one pang, or several pangs.
fact: «Pang» means a sudden sharp pain or a sudden strong feeling.
fact: «Hunger pangs» are sudden pains in your stomach when you are very hungry.
fact: «A pang of guilt» means a sudden feeling that you have done something wrong.
fact: «A pang of regret» means a sudden feeling of being sorry about something.
exercise: «As the music ended, Lara felt a pang of sadness.» What is a pang here? | A slow walk | A loud noise | A kind of cake | *A sudden strong feeling
exercise: Ben's tummy gave a sudden pang before lunch. What does pang mean? | A loud laugh | *A sudden sharp pain | A sleepy yawn | A cold drink
exercise: «She felt a pang of guilt after lying to her mum.» What was the pang about? | Winning a race | Getting a new pet | Going to the park | *Doing something wrong
test: «A pang of hunger hit Priya just before tea.» What does a pang of hunger suggest? | A feeling of being full | Sleeping very late | A kind of hat | *A sudden strong feeling of being hungry
test: Which phrase means a sudden feeling of being sorry? | A pang of morning | A pang of rain | *A pang of regret | A pang of sleep
exam: Which word fills the gap? «Ella had sharp ___ of hunger before dinner.» | *pangs | panging | pang | pangly
